findings.body:
The five `${{ steps.review.outputs.* }}` values here are runtime-generated fixed strings (enum policy names, integers), not attacker-controlled PR content — so this is not the injection pattern, just the pattern the repo otherwise avoids for copy-paste examples. Routing them through an `env:` block keeps `examples/` consistent with the posture documented for workflows and prevents drift if a future output ever carries PR-derived text.

```suggestion
      - name: IAR cost telemetry
        if: always() && steps.review.outputs.iteration-round != ''
        env:
          IAR_GENERATION: ${{ steps.review.outputs.iteration-generation }}
          IAR_ROUND: ${{ steps.review.outputs.iteration-round }}
          IAR_POLICY: ${{ steps.review.outputs.iteration-policy-applied }}
          IAR_COST: ${{ steps.review.outputs.iteration-cost-vs-baseline-estimate }}
        run: |
          echo "::notice title=IAR::gen=$IAR_GENERATION round=$IAR_ROUND policy=$IAR_POLICY cost=$IAR_COST"
```
